      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Development of the MAO-inhibitors has been an important advance in the treatment of tuberculosis, mental depression, several of the collagen diseases, hypertension and angina pectoris. Treatment must be carefully controlled and individualized. A sufficient number of MAO-inhibitors is available at present to afford ready and correct selection of the proper one for a given patient and disease. Provided such care is observed, treatment is most successful and side effects are few and, as a rule, readily corrected."},
